# Regenerable build products. Unanchored, so the rule matches at every depth:
# trybuild resolves its scratch project against the *test crate's* manifest
# directory and writes `probe/target/tests/trybuild/` whatever `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`
# the run sets, which an anchored `/target/` does not cover — the recorded
# invocation left 763 MB of it untracked in `git status`.
#
# The retained `.stderr` goldens beside each fixture are the evidence and stay
# tracked; `Cargo.lock` stays tracked too, because the goldens depend on which
# `trybuild` normalized them.
target/
